# Prisma and migrations

- Ask the user before adding or changing a migration.
- Create migrations with `npx prisma migrate dev --name <snake_case>` against
  the local database. Never edit a migration that is already on `main`; add a
  new one instead.
- Never run `prisma migrate reset`, `prisma db push`, or any command against a
  production `DATABASE_URL`. Production applies migrations only through the
  deploy script, right after a database backup.
- Keep migrations backward compatible with the release still running: add
  nullable columns or defaults first, backfill, then tighten in a later
  release. Dropping or renaming needs a maintenance window (see
  `docs/deployment/VPS.md`).
- After a schema change run `npx prisma validate`, `npm run typecheck`, and
  `npm run test:integration`; `scripts/setup-test-db.sh` applies migrations to
  the local test database.
- User IDs in PostgreSQL are MongoDB Auth.js user IDs stored as strings. There
  is no cross-database foreign key; do not add one.
